docs {
  # Customer Portal
  
  Create Stripe Customer Portal session URL.
  
  ## Endpoint
  POST /api/subscriptions/customer-portal
  
  ## Authentication
  **Required** - Must include Bearer token in Authorization header
  
  ## Description
  Creates a URL to access Stripe Customer Portal where users can:
  - View billing history
  - Update credit card information
  - Download invoices
  - Update customer details (name, address, phone, shipping, tax ID)
  
  ## Preconditions
  - User must have an active subscription (status: 'active' or 'trialing')
  - currentPeriodEnd must be >= current date
  - Must have stripeCustomerId
  
  ## Response (200 OK)
  ```json
  {
    "url": "https://billing.stripe.com/p/session/..."
  }
  ```
  
  - `url`: Stripe Customer Portal URL
  
  ## Error Responses
  - **400 Bad Request**:
    - `{ "message": "noActiveSubscription" }` - No active subscription or missing customer ID
  - **401 Unauthorized**: Missing or invalid token
  
  ## Business Logic
  - Portal configuration is created once and cached
  - Allows updating: name, address, phone, shipping, tax_id
  - Session is temporary and expires
  
  ## Use Cases
  - Manage payment information
  - View billing history
  - Update customer details
  - Download invoices
}
